# Backups on {{ inventory_hostname }} — quick reference

Full guide: {{ restic_readme_url }}

- Repo (primary): `{{ restic_repository }}`
{% if _restic_secondary_enabled %}
- Repo (secondary): `{{ restic_secondary_repository }}` — for any command below, source `env.secondary` instead of `env`
{% endif %}

## Load the environment (once per shell)
```bash
set -a; . {{ restic_config_dir }}/env; set +a
{% if _restic_secondary_enabled %}
set -a; . {{ restic_config_dir }}/env.secondary; set +a
{% endif %}
```

## Status / confirm backups are working
```bash
{% if restic_scheduler == "systemd" %}
systemctl list-timers 'restic-*'                       # next/last run of every job
journalctl --since '24 hours ago' -u 'restic-*'        # recent run output
journalctl -fu restic-backup.service                   # follow a live backup
{% else %}
ls -lt {{ restic_log_dir }}/                           # latest logs first
tail -F {{ restic_log_dir }}/*.log                     # follow live output
{% endif %}
restic snapshots --latest 5                            # 5 most recent backups (shows backed-up paths)
restic stats latest                                    # size & file count of latest
restic check                                           # verify repo integrity (metadata)
```

## Back up now
```bash
{% if restic_scheduler == "systemd" %}
systemctl start restic-backup.service && journalctl -fu restic-backup.service
{% else %}
{{ restic_config_dir }}/restic-backup.sh
{% endif %}
```

## Restore (always preview first)
```bash
restic restore latest --target /tmp/preview --dry-run --verbose=2       # preview, writes nothing
restic restore latest --target /var/restore                             # whole snapshot into a sandbox
restic restore latest --target /var/restore --include /etc/somefile     # one path
restic restore <snapshot-id> --target /var/restore                      # a specific snapshot (id from `restic snapshots`)
restic dump latest /etc/somefile > /tmp/somefile                        # stream a single file
```

Browse the repo like a filesystem (read-only):
```bash
mkdir -p /mnt/restic && restic mount /mnt/restic &     # then ls /mnt/restic/snapshots/latest/
fusermount -u /mnt/restic                              # unmount when done
```

Restore into a fresh directory, never on top of live data. More: {{ restic_readme_url }}
